Digital Prioris LX Servers

Highlights

*  Affordable Pentium based servers with all of the "hot options" normally
   found on higher-end systems
*  Designed to easily expand

Product description

The Prioris LX servers are the new entry level servers in the Prioris line.
The Prioris LX servers feature leading-edge technology like PCI and a high
level of onboard integrated functionality:  graphics, Ethernet controller,
PCI EIDE, and Fast Narrow SCSI-2. As users' requirements grow, so can the
Prioris LX, offering upgrades on video memory, system memory, cache,
expansion capability, and storage. The Prioris LX is also uniprocessor
upgradable via a daughtercard to the future Intel processors. The server can
be rackmounted using Digital's rackmount system. (See related article in
this issue.)

The Prioris LX servers deliver affordability, manageability and superior
Pentium performance at a great price. The Prioris LX servers are the ideal
entry level servers for price-sensitive small-to-medium sized businesses and
workgroups. Also, with Digital's Remote Server Management software, the
Prioris LX can be the solution for remote locations and branch offices.

Benefits

*  Reliability and expansion--Internal and external SCSI devices, onboard
   Ethernet, graphics, PCI EIDE, Fast Narrow SCSI-2, optional synchronous
   cache for higher performance, password and chassis security, and optional
   ECC memory
*  Compatibility  Certified on all major operating systems for a range of
   applications support
*  Superior support--Three year on-site warranty, with next business day
   response

Availability and ordering

The Prioris LX servers are available now.  Option and part numbers supported
on the Prioris LX can be found in the PC Product and Configuration Guide,
part number EC-N5194-88.

