New Digital HiNote and HiNote Ultra Notebooks

Highlights

*  Latest members of the Digital HiNote family extend industry-leading
   Notebook PCs
*  Mobile Media Module offers industry's most feature-packed media module

Product description

Digital HiNote and HiNote Ultra are notebooks designed to meet the needs of
the very mobile professional with the sleekest form factor, the lightest
weight, and highest performance with rich features.

New Digital HiNote System

The Digital HiNote CS475 provides mobile professionals with a slim and light
full-featured notebook. This model introduces a 9.5-inch color Dual Scan LCD
panel paired with a DX4-75 MHz processor and 510 MB hard disk drive to
provide the best performance at an attractive price. HiNote averages 21
percent smaller and 12 percent lighter than full-featured competitive
notebooks in its class.

Digital HiNote Ultra Systems

The new HiNote Ultra CS475 and CT475 systems continue to deliver on the
promise of "no compromise" computing, with no sacrifice for users in terms
of weight, size, speed, storage, and raw computing power. With 528 MB hard
disk drive capacity, these systems deliver a new standard of performance in
notebook computers and are, on average, 24 percent smaller and 11 percent
lighter than other systems in its class.

The Digital HiNote Ultra 528 MB Hard Disk Drive factory upgrade provides
optimum expandability for any user of a HiNote Ultra system. The upgrade is
offered exclusively through Digital's Multivendor Customer Services (MCS).

Digital HiNote Ultra Mobile Media Module

The HiNote Ultra Mobile Media Module, when combined with the ultra light
HiNote Ultra, offers the industry's thinnest, most feature-packed detachable
Mobile Media Module available. It incorporates 16-bit Stereo Audio sound, 2X
CD-ROM, three full-range stereo speakers, joystick/MIDI port, audio line out
and line in, and volume range controls. The Ultra Mobile Media Module weighs
just 2 pounds and is just .8-inch high. With the Ultra attached, it is a
sleek 6 pounds and 2-inch package that is an average of 45 percent smaller
and 38 percent lighter than other systems in its class.

