StorageWorks RAID Array 230 Subsystem for PC Networks

Highlights

*  Hardware RAID subsystem for Intel systems with PCI bus running Novell
   NetWare or Microsoft Windows NT
*  PCI backplane RAID controller provides RAID levels 0 (striping), 1
   (mirroring), 0+1 (striped mirroring), 5 (striping with parity), and JBOD
*  Supports both 8 bit (narrow) and 16 bit (wide) drives
*  Higher performance than the EISA based StorageWorks RAID Array 210
   subsystem

Product description

The StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem is the newest member of the
StorageWorks RAID Array 200 family. It is functionally identical to the
StorageWorks RAID Array 210 subsystem, but utilizes a PCI backplane RAID
controller instead of the EISA backplane RAID controller. The RAID utilities
and the documentation are common to both products, providing great
flexibility in implementing RAID systems across the enterprise.

A StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem is comprised of a PCI backplane RAID
controller, operating system specific RAID drivers and utilities (software),
documentation, and disk drives with appropriate cables and enclosures.

Benefits

*  Provides a cost-effective, high-availability, and high performance RAID
   solution for Intel system platforms using an industry-standard PCI bus
*  User-selectable RAID levels plus the ability to mix RAID levels within a
   given drive group
*  Allows users to tailor the StorageWorks 230 RAID subsystem to specific
   performance, fault tolerance, or availability needs

Product positioning

*  The RAID Array 230 offers significant improvement in performance (27
   percent higher transfer rate and 34 percent higher I/O rate) at a
   higher price point.
*  The RAID Array 230 supports both narrow and wide drives.
*  The RAID Array 230 uses the same graphical user interface and offers the
   same features as the RAID Array 210.

Availability and ordering

The StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem is available pre-configured with
three disk drives, or can be configured by a sum of the pieces scheme that
vastly reduces the number of orderable parts, and provides growth and
configuration flexibility.

A StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem consists of the following key
components:

*  A SWIKX PCI backplane RAID controller, which includes the Novell NetWare
   and Windows NT drivers and configuration utilities, cables (both narrow
   wide), and documentation
*  StorageWorks disk drives
*  StorageWorks enclosure(s)
*  Additional StorageWorks components (redundant power supplies)

The SWIKX backplane RAID controller is available in two models: a single
SCSI channel variant that supports up to 7 disk drives, and a three channel
model that supports up to 21 drives.

