Performance

The performance of a RAID subsystem is dependent on a large number of
parameters, including RAID level, RAID subsystem specific attributes (type
and size of cache), number of RAID controllers on the system, number and
type of disks used, application parameters (read/write ratio, file size, and
block size, etc.), type of system, overall system activity, operating
system, and many other features.

Performance testing in a user environment indicates that the performance of
an EISA based  StorageWorks RAID Array 210 subsystem ranges from 150 to 350
I/Os per second for an application using a balanced mix of read and writes
in a RAID 5 configuration. Preliminary tests indicate that in the same
environment, the PCI based StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem provides
performance in the range of 300 to 700 I/Os per second (doubling the
performance of the RAID Array 210 subsystem).

