MailWorks for UNIX V1.7

Highlights

*  Improved memory management and TeamLinks Macintosh support
*  Supports the XMR gateway to Message Router
*  MailWorks Motif Client for SunOS now available
*  New integrated directory lookup for Motif clients

Product description

MailWorks for UNIX V1.7 is a mail server that supports a variety of mail
clients, including TeamLinks for Windows and Macintosh, Microsoft Mail for
Windows, Lotus cc:Mail for Windows, and MailWorks Clients for DOS and Motif
( Digital UNIX and SunOS) software.

The MailWorks server offers a choice of messaging transports such as
built-in connectivity to Digital UNIX sendmail, which provides a seamless
connection to the Internet and other SMTP environments. MailWorks connects
directly to Digital's leadership X.400 Message Transport Agent, MAILbus 400,
and Digital's X.500 Directory Services. In addition, MailWorks software can
exchange messages with Digital's VAXmail software. MAILbus 400 and DEC X.500
Directory Service are optional products that are purchased and installed
separately.

MailWorks for UNIX V1.7 is factory installed on three Internet AlphaServer
packages. These packages offer a choice of AlphaServer system and a
comprehensive set of factory installed pre-packaged Internet software and
system utilities. New features:

*  MailWorks V1.7 adds support for the XMR gateway. This allows users to
   send mail to MailWorks for OpenVMS or ALL-IN-1 users on Message Router
   systems. To use the XMR gateway, users require both MAILbus 400 and the
   XMR gateway to Message Router.

*  The MailWorks Motif Client now includes an integrated directory lookup
   capability that allows users to access local or X.500 directories.

*  V1.7 includes improvements to the memory management module, which
   minimizes memory usage. The software also includes an improved
   installation procedure; improvements have been made to increase
   reliability and offer higher performance.

*  A new MailWorks Motif Client for SunOS software is available. This client
   is consistent with the existing UNIX Motif client, including the new
   integrated directory lookup feature. The MailWorks Motif Client for SunOS
   software requires SunOS 4.1.3 with Patch Levels, Open Windows V3.0
   100444-58, and a suitable Sun workstation with at least 32 MB of memory.
   The Sun workstation must be connected to the MailWorks Server Node via
   TCP/IP. The MailWorks Motif Client for SunOS software is packaged with
   the MailWorks CD-ROM and can be installed via the network. A MailWorks
   Motif Client for SunOS license is required for each individual
   workstation.

*  The MailWorks Motif Client for SunOS license is operating system
   independent.  This means that users who purchase a license for the Sun
   client and install it on a workstation running SunOS software can upgrade
   to Solaris software in the future, when the MailWorks Motif Client for
   Solaris software is available - without needing to buy a new license. The
   user must purchase the necessary media and license updates for the new
   versions.

Availability and ordering

The MailWorks for UNIX V1.7 media kit is available now. MailWorks for UNIX
V1.7 has been included with the Internet AlphaServer system and with the
Digital UNIX Layered Products Consolidated Distribution CD-ROM. The
MailWorks Motif Client for SunOS software is only available with the
MailWorks V1.7 media kit.

