Intel's Pentium 120 MHz Processor Added to Celebris XL

Digital has added Intel's fastest processor, the Pentium 120 MHz chip, to
its Celebris XL desktop PC, creating the new Celebris XL 5120. The new
Celebris XL model is Digital's first system utilizing Intel's 120 MHz
Pentium processor, and the only machine offering CISC-to-RISC upgradability
through a 233 MHz Alpha microprocessor. Because of its fast speed, the
Pentium 120 MHz processor does not support dual processing at this time.
Digital will offer a dual processing configuration and a dual processor
upgrade when these are available from Intel.

Designed for performance-intensive applications, the Celebris XL family
combines the strengths of the XL CPU upgradable daughter card architecture
with the ease-of-use features standard in all Digital desktop PCs. The
family, including the new Celebris XL 5120, provides the widest range of
operating system and network operating system support available.

The Celebris XL 5120 models are available now through Digital and its
business partners. Options supported on the Celebris XL series can be found
in Digital's PC Product Configuration Guide.

