510 MB Hard Disk for Digital HiNote Notebooks

The thin, sleek, and lightweight Digital HiNote system (on average 21
percent smaller and 12 percent lighter than its competitors) now comes in a
510 MB hard disk model. Users who require a notebook with large disk
capacity no longer need to compromise on size and weight. With the 510 MB
model of the Digital HiNote CT475, a user can purchase over one-half GB of
disk space in a system that weighs less than five pounds.  Also, existing
HiNote users can upgrade their present notebooks with the user upgradable
510 MB hard disk kit. The new 510 MB hard disk model and upgrade kit are
available now through Digital and its business partners. The hard disk drive
upgrade kit requires that DOS and Windows be pre-installed by the user. To
transfer current hard disk drive applications and data, users need to
back-up the entire contents of their current system hard drive via floppy
diskettes, tape drive, or a network. They then install the new 510 MB drive
and load information from the back-up source. Some users may prefer having a
local reseller perform this function for them.

