Digital Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 -- Desktop PCs with Pentium Power

Highlights

*  The Venturis Pentium series includes 24 models ranging from 75 MHz to 100
   MHz Pentium-based desktop PCs, allowing users a choice of computing power
   and performance
*  Key features include: EPA Energy Star compliance with advanced power
   management, Enhanced IDE on the PCI local bus, 64-bit accelerated
   Desktop Management Interface (DMI) readiness, integrated Plug and Play
   BIOS

Product description

The Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 slimline and full-profile (VenturisFP)
desktop PCs deliver solid price/performance in the most demanding corporate
and small-to-medium business, education, and government environments. The
new Venturis PCs are for the volume purchaser in small, medium, and large
organizations. They meet the performance requirements of the general
business user as well as the MIS professional who needs to confidently
deploy an industry-standard desktop personal computer into an existing
environment -- with the least amount of technical support, at the lowest
possible cost.

Specifically, the Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 slimline and full profile
models are designed for:

*  General business users looking for solid system performance, PCI/ISA
   flexibility, advanced power management, and industry-standard
   expandability and upgradability.
*  MIS administrators requiring a desktop standard for national and
   worldwide distribution and deployment.
*  Technically proficient users running demanding business applications,
   such as financial analysis, CAD, desktop publishing, imaging, and
   multimedia.
*  General business users anticipating a strategic desktop migration to
   Microsoft Windows 95, Windows NT 3.5 Workstation, and the next generation
   of 32-bit Windows-based applications.
*  LAN managers requiring a standards-based solution that meets the
   challenge of linking PC platforms, components, management applications,
   and peripherals.

These new systems provide an optimum balance of 64-bit accelerated PCI
graphics, a 64-bit data path to system RAM and secondary cache, and powerful
Intel Pentium processors for general office applications such as word
processing, spreadsheets, presentation graphics, database management, and
communications. Hard drive options include 420 MB, 540 MB, 845 MB, or 1.2 GB
IDE (Integrated Device Electronics) drives. System memory features a base of
8 MB, expandable to 128 MB with industry-standard 4, 8, 16, 32 and 64 MB
SIMMs. Each system is pre-installed with MS-DOS 6.22 and Windows for
Workgroups 3.11.

Other Venturis features include an Enhanced local bus IDE subsystem--a
faster interface to the hard drive for better data throughput and improved
productivity, accelerated graphics performance, Plug and Play ready
integration, multi-level security, and a three-year limited warranty.

All Digital Venturis models are Desktop Management Interface (DMI) ready,
which will provide significant advancements in the network administration of
an organization's client/server computing environment. The Venturis DMI
allows desktop client hardware and software status reporting, asset
management across a network, remote diagnostics of client PCs, and improved
management of a company's enterprisewide, distributed computing environment.

Digital has focused on how users interact with their computers. From the new
Getting Started user interface and Quick Setup Guide to the uniquely
designed easy access enclosure, the Venturis Pentium series is designed to
provide easy access to product and service information -- enabling LAN
administrators and resellers to get users' systems set-up and running
quickly. The PCs have gone through Digital's highest levels of desktop
testing procedures, assuring industry-standard compatibility and
reliability. In addition, all Venturis desktop PCs support the U.S.
Environmental Protection Agency's standard for Energy Star compliance.

