Benefits

*  Pentium 75 MHz, 90 MHz, and 100 MHz processor performance is available in
   both slimline and full profile Venturis models.
*  Zero Insertion Force (ZIF) socket is upgradable to Intel's future
   OverDrive processors based on Pentium processor technology.
*  64-bit accelerated graphics on the PCI local bus provides superior
   graphics performance.
*  With up to 128 MB of system memory, the Venturis Pentium series provides
   expansion and flexibility for new applications and emerging technologies.
*  Enhanced IDE on the PCI local bus allows attachment of four IDE devices,
   such as hard disk drives, CD-ROM, or tape drive for increased performance
   and expandability.
*  256 KB of secondary writeback cache enhances system performance for
   processor-intensive application environments.
*  1 MB of graphics memory is standard, expandable to 2 MB for more colors
   and higher resolutions.
*  Plug and Play ready support makes the desktop system more versatile and
   easier to use.
*  U.S. EPA Energy Star compliance reduces energy costs.
*  Digital's Getting Started user interface privides easy access to product
   and service information.
*  Comprehensive multi-level security is provided.
*  Flashable BIOS features multilingual capabilities.
*  The new PCs comply with worldwide safety and emissions regulations.
*  A three-year limited warranty stands behind Digital quality and
   engineering, as well as Digital's worldwide service and support centers.

Product positioning

Digital's Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 slimline and full profile models
replace the Celebris 466, 4100, and 560, and the Venturis 560 models. The
Digital Venturis line is positioned according to price/performance and
functionality. Processors range from 486 to Pentium processors, with PCI/ISA
bus architecture on the Pentium models and ISA bus architecture on the 486
models. All Venturis systems feature local bus accelerated graphics
performance; Enhanced IDE on the local bus; industry-standard Plug and Play,
Windows 95, and DMI ready support; and a unique system design focused on
usability for user set-up, installation, and upgradability.

