High resolutions and color depth

All Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 models feature True Color graphics providing
up to 16.8 million colors--as many colors as the eye can see. True Color
gives users the ability to display photo-realistic images. To take full
advantage of True Color images and today's higher Windows resolution modes,
the Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 sport a full 1 MB of graphics memory, which
can be easily upgraded to 2 MB for even faster graphics performance.

Expansion slots

Venturis slimline 575, 590, and 5100 models feature three industry-standard
expansion slots: one full-size ISA slot, one full-size PCI/ISA shared slot,
and one half-size PCI slot. VenturisFP 575, 590, and 5100 models feature
five industry-standard expansion slots: three full-size ISA slots, one
full-size PCI/ISA shared slot, and one half-size PCI slot. The Venturis 575,
590, and 5100 dual bus architecture provides users with the flexibility
required for today's PCI and ISA adapter environments.

Enhanced local bus IDE

All Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 slimline and full profile models feature
dual channel Enhanced IDE. This allows each model to support up to four IDE
devices (two high-speed devices on the PCI local bus channel and two devices
on the ISA bus channel) and connectivity to hard disk drives with storage
capacity greater than 528 MB.

The biggest advantage of Enhanced IDE is performance; its Mode 3 transfer
supports a fast 11.1 MB-per-second data transfer rate. In addition, Enhanced
IDE provides 32-bit wide data transfers between the disk device driver and
the IDE interface, as well as support for block-mode transfers.

Integrated I/O ports

Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 models contain two buffered high-speed serial
ports that utilize a fast 16550 UART to support transfer rates up to 19.2 Kb
per second. The enhanced parallel port supports the new Enhanced
Capabilities Port (ECP), Enhanced Parallel Port (EPP), standard Centronics,
and PS/2 bi-directional specifications.The combination of high-performance
(buffered) serial ports and an enhanced parallel port will ensure optimum
performance with the next generation of peripherals and operating systems.

Device bays

The Venturis 575, 590, and 5100 slimline models feature two externally
accessible device bays: one 3.5 inch device bay occupied with a standard
3.5-inch 1.44-MB diskette drive, and one available 5.25-inch by 1.6-inch
high bay. The slimline models also feature two internal 3.5-inch by 1.0-inch
high hard disk drive bays (models with a hard drive have one bay configured
with standard IDE hard disk drive and one open/available hard disk drive
bay).

The VenturisFP 575, 590, and 5100 models feature three externally accessible
device bays: one 3.5-inch device bay occupied with a standard 3.5-inch
