POLYCENTER Performance Advisor and Advisor Collector V3.0 for Digital UNIX

Highlights

*  Performance tuning and advisor capabilities are now available for the
   Digital UNIX operating system
*  Enhanced performance data collection capabilities are now available for
   Digital UNIX systems

Product description

The POLYCENTER Performance Solution is a set of layered products that
collects system data from OpenVMS and UNIX based systems, and then uses that
data to provide performance management. The products, including POLYCENTER
Performance Advisor and POLYCENTER Advisor Collector, can be used both with
standalone and networked systems.

Users require performance management software to understand, optimize, and
tune existing system configurations. Typically, this involves changing
system parameters, reconfiguring workloads, tuning applications, and the
like. The POLYCENTER Performance Solution family significantly reduces the
time and effort required to optimize current and future configurations and
right-size system resources  -- at the right time and for the right cost.

V3.0 features

The POLYCENTER Performance Advisor makes recommendations for improving
system performance by analyzing system data through expert system
technology, identifying specific conditions causing performance degradation,
and presenting detailed evidence to support its conclusions. Now available
for Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) systems, the software includes:

*  Performance knowledge base and customizable rules for expert tuning
   advice
*  Performance analysis and reporting
*  Performance characteristics displayed in graphs, pie charts, and bar
   charts

The Performance Advisor analyzes statistics and parameters collected from
each node by the enhanced Advisor Collector for Digital UNIX software to
determine whether specific conditions are contributing to system performance
degradation. Based on its findings, the Performance Advisor recommends ways
to improve system performance and provides evidence to support its
conclusions. The Performance Advisor can organize information into several
different reports that:

*    Identify system resource limitations for the workload when they exist.
*    Identify system parameter settings that may be adding to system
     overhead or degrading system performance.
*    Evaluate trends in system performance.
*    Evaluate the effects of changes in workload and configuration
     characteristics.

The Performance Advisor allows report and graph generation using either the
GUI or command line interface. With the command line interface, users can
employ POLYCENTER Scheduler to generate these reports and graphs for
management updates, periodically or on a regular basis.

The POLYCENTER Performance Advisor also provides customized rule based
alarming whereby the Advisor, running in the background, can continuously
monitor multiple systems and check the performance parameters against both
factory defined and user defined rules, and send alarms when any of the rule
conditions are met. The alarm notification can be done using Internet mail,
SNMP traps, console messages, or invocation of user defined shell scripts.
Internet mail can be sent to a list of mail addresses. SNMP traps allow
alert notification to POLYCENTER NetView and other SNMP management
applications. Console messages allow notification to the console operator or
to console management applications such as the POLYCENTER Console Manager.
User defined shell scripts allow users to run applications or command
procedures required to take specific actions, including automatic corrective
actions based on individual rules.

Benefits

POLYCENTER Performance Advisor helps system managers perform typically
inexpensive tasks that improve system performance. By performing these tasks
on a regular basis, users achieve a consistent level of performance and
optimize their Digital investment.

Availability and ordering

POLYCENTER Performance Advisor (SPD 64.08) and POLYCENTER Advisor Collector
(SPD 64.22) are available through Digital, its DECdirect service, and its
business partners.  The products will be included on the Consolidated
Distribution CD-ROM, with documentation on the Online Documentation CD-ROM.
The Performance Advisor resides on a server and collects data from all
Digital UNIX systems running the Advisor Collector. Each system from which
the user wants to collect data requires a licensed Advisor Collector to pass
data to the Performance Advisor. The Performance Advisor does not currently
use data collected by the Digital UNIX, ULTRIX, AIX, SunOS, and Solaris Data
Collectors, which work with the POLYCENTER Performance Monitor.

