POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem V1.1 for OpenVMS

Highlights

*    Support for OpenVMS Alpha V6.2 and OpenVMS VAX V6.2
*    Integration with Media and Device Management Services V2.5B, allowing
     use in the same system environment as Storage Library System V2.5B, and
     POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Management V1.1.

Product description

POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem V1.1 for OpenVMS systems (SPD 46.40)
supports OpenVMS VAX V6.1 and 6.2, and OpenVMS Alpha V6.2. This release also
includes support for Media and Device Management Services V2.5B.

This layered software product allows users and applications to manipulate
tape files using the same interface currently used to manipulate files on
magnetic disk. OpenVMS utilities, such as COPY and DIRECTORY, work
seamlessly with this product. Applications that use RMS sequential access or
OpenVMS high level language sequential input-output routines can read and
write directly to files on tape.

This release is integrated with Media and Device Management Services V2.5B,
which allows the installation of Storage Library System V2.5B, POLYCENTER
Archive/Backup V1.0, and POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Management V1.1 on
the same system. Media and Device Management Services V2.5B allows these
storage management software products to share use of the storage resources
without contention. This includes sharing of high capacity devices such as
the TL series of Digital Linear Tape (DLT) libraries.

For more information, see the "POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem for
OpenVMS VAX V1.0" article in the April 1995 issue of Customer Update.

Benefits

POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem allows users with large files to
access these files directly on tape, without the need for more expensive and
limited capacity magnetic media.

Traditional strategies, based on operator-attended backup with file
restoration on demand, and strategies that depend on users managing their
own tape catalogs and media fail due to high cost and low productivity.
Organizations often collect thousands of tapes filled with user files that
are unidentified and difficult to maintain. Users may spend days of their
time and tie up entire tape libraries searching for a specific file they
have lost.

POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem V1.1 for OpenVMS systems provides the
following benefits:

*    Allows users to focus on their applications tasks, instead of media
     management and cataloging.
*    Makes using tapes as easy as using disks--at a fraction of the cost.
*    Enhances productivity by minimizing user training and application
     modification due to its transparency, ease of use, and media management
     capabilities.
*    Eliminates much of the system administration associated with user
     requests for tape mounts and file recovery.

Availability and ordering

POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem V1.1 is available now through Digital
and its business partners.

