CBL_A VAX DIBOL to ANSI C Translator

Highlights

*    Converts VAX DIBOL based applications to ANSI C
*    Changes proprietary legacy applications into open applications
*    Supports multiple platforms and operating systems

Product description

CBL software is a sophisticated conversion tool that enables developers to
easily convert their VAX DIBOL based applications to ANSI C. The product
offers a mechanism for creating portable C code based on existing VAX DIBOL
source code, preserving the user's investment in application design and
development. CBL software enables developers to broaden the appeal of their
VAX DIBOL applications by converting them to a portable, open language--
while continuing to maintain them in the VAX DIBOL code. The translator
software also helps developers transition to the C programming language
quickly and effectively.

Benefits

*  Expands the range of platforms upon which applications will run by making
   the application source code portable.
*  Protects investments in application design and development by converting
   existing code; no rewriting required.
*  Enables developers to move away from VAX DIBOL as a development language
   and into C without throwing out existing VAX DIBOL applications.
*  Allows a smooth transition into the C development environment.
*  Enables users to employ existing VAX DIBOL code as a tool to train
   programmers in C programming.
*  Allows users to avoid the runtime license costs associated with other
   solutions.

The industry trend is toward businesses equipped with multiple platforms
running multiple operating systems. However, users with applications based
on proprietary programming languages have often made a large investment in
these proprietary systems, which are still useful. CBL software allows
useful legacy applications to be rejuvenated and made available on a wide
range of platforms. For example, the CBL translator could be used to port a
set of VAX VMS based DIBOL applications to a network with Alpha systems
running OpenVMS Alpha software, servers running Windows NT software, and PCs
running Windows and MS-DOS software.

Availability and ordering

CBL products and services can be ordered in the Americas from Migration
Specialties International (phone: 719-687-9196; fax: 719-687-8747; Internet
address: claremont@isvsrv.enet.dec.com), and in Europe and Asia Pacific from
Amethyst Computer Resources, Ltd. (phone: [44] 1530812458; fax: [44] 510073;
Internet address: john@amethyst.demon.uk).

CBL software currently available for converting VAX DIBOL applications
includes:

*    CBL for Converting to OpenVMS Alpha
*    CBL for Converting to MS-DOS
*    CBL for Converting to Windows 3.1
*    CBL for Converting to Windows NT
*    CBL for Converting to SCO UNIX
*    CBL Demonstration Kit

Services

MSI offers a complete range of customized migration services to assist VAX
DIBOL users in converting their code to C, including:

*    Migration feasibility studies
*    Code conversion
*    Onsite installation services
*    User training
*    Project planning
*    Code optimization
*    Quality assurance testing
*    Post-migration support

