the Alpha 21164 chip. The AlphaStation 600 family is housed in a mid-tower
enclosure with a capacity of up to 1 GB of ECC memory,  6 internal storage
slots for up to 17.2 GB of SCSI disk, and 8 total option slots that accept
PCI and EISA options available from both Digital and its business partners.
The new workstation is ideal for users who demand high performance and
graphics, and require all the benefits of industry-standard option support.

The system supports Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) and OpenVMS software.
Microsoft's Windows NT environment will be supported in the fourth quarter
of 1995. Designed for overall balanced performance, the AlphaStation 600
5/266 and 5/300 include on-board cache (either 2 MB or 4 MB on the 5/266; 4
MB on the 5/300) , a 256-bit wide memory bus, and the first-in-the-industry
64-bit workstation PCI I/O bus that runs at 264 MB per second at peak.

The AlphaStation 600 delivers leadership CPU performance:

*    Model 5/266 -- 288 SPECint92 and 428 SPECfp92
*    Model 5/300  -- 334 SPECint92 and 503 SPECfp92

The AlphaStation 600 workstation family is multimedia ready, offering
multiple video options and supporting built-in collaboration software. Users
can easily add video capture for video conferencing or multimedia authoring
with the new FullVideo Supreme video input/output PCI option for Digital
UNIX based systems (see the "Video Capture Options and Desktop Camera for
AlphaStation Systems" article in this issue ).

Upgrade to Model 5/300

The AlphaStation 600 5/266 to AlphaStation 600 5/300 upgrade package will
ship in the fourth quarter of this calendar year. It will be a board swap
that Digital`s field service will handle. The upgrade, whch has a single
part number, will include a new 4 MB cache as well as the 300 MHz Alpha
21164. Users who want the 300 MHz system can take delivery of the
AlphaStation 600 5/266 immediately and get the upgrade when it becomes
available later this year. The upgrade is a no-penalty upgrade, meaning that
when the AlphaStation 600 5/300 begins shipping, Digital will not price it
below the sum of today's AlphaStation 600 5/266 and the 5/300 upgrade.

Application Availability

All applications that now run on AlphaStation workstations (such as
ZLXp-E1/E2/E3 graphics) will run on the AlphaStation 600 family.
Applications using higher level graphics than ZLXp-E3 may need
recertification. Applications will run faster without recompilation.
However, maximum speed-ups will require recompilation.

BENEFITS

*  Performance--Supports the most compute and graphics intensive
   applications in technical environments, including MCAD, ECAD (Electronic
   Computer Aided Design), geographic information systems, science and
   research, and technical CASE.

*  Investment protection--Binary compatible with the Alpha family; eight I/O
   slots for a variety of PCI/EISA options; and the industry's best
   warranty.

*  Price--Delivers leadership performance at a mid-range price.

*  Open system--Offers industry standard PCI/EISA options and a choice of
   operating systems available through a variety of suppliers.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

The AlphaStation 600 family will replace the DEC 3000 upper mid-range to
high-end TURBOchannel based workstations, offering users continued unmatched
UNIX and OpenVMS price/performance leadership in the $30,000 to $50,000
range.

