UNIX Package Option for AlphaStation 200 4/100 Workstation

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Entry level UNIX only AlphaStation 200 4/100 desktop package option
*  Improved UNIX performance with V3.2C of Digital UNIX
*  Three-year hardware warranty and 90-day telephone advisory software
   support included

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The new UNIX only package option for the AlphaStation 200 4/100 64-bit Alpha
workstation offers exceptional performance at an affordable entry price and
sets the standard for entry level pricing and price/performance in UNIX
workstations. As with all of the AlphaStation 200 family members, the UNIX
entry level package accepts industry-standard options running on both PCI
and ISA buses. This package option comes with 24 MB of memory, 535 MB disk,
ATI mach64 graphics, 15-inch color monitor, and factory installed Digital
UNIX V3.2C (formerly called DEC OSF/1) providing improved performance and
the most value for your investment.

V3.2C is the next release of the Digital UNIX operating system, which
supports the full line of Alpha systems and provides complete binary
compatibility for applications currently running on V3.2. V3.2C includes
maintenance bug fixes, supports new hardware platform variants, adds new
device support (such as PCI ATM and PCI Fast Ethernet), and provides system
resource utilization improvements that are especially beneficial to low-end,
memory constrained applications. With V3.2C, Digital UNIX now supports a 24
MB entry level Alpha workstation.

BENEFITS

*  Performance--Supports today's leading applications in both technical
   (MCAD, ECAD, and CASE) and commercial (desktop publishing, office
   productivity, finance, and database) environments.

*  Price--Exceptional dollars per SPECmark for UNIX systems.

*  Investment protection--Provides future upgradability to more powerful CPU
   chips and offers the industry's best warranty.

*  Open system--Industry-standard PCI/ISA options available through a
   variety of suppliers.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The UNIX only AlphaStation 200 4/100 system can be ordered now and will
begin shipping on July 30, 1995. This package variant supports Digital UNIX
V3.2C (or later). The operating system is factory installed. Factory
installed software is not a substitute for media and documentation. Users
should order the required media and documentation kit as a separate line
item. At least one media and documentation kit per site is recommended.

All options ordered with packaged systems will be factory installed unless
specified as spares. All systems shipped from manufacturing are set to 240
volts, and may be reset by the user as required to 120 or 240V. The system
packages do not include a keyboard or power cord. These country-specific
items should be ordered separately.

The AlphaStation 200 4/100 Digital UNIX entry level package includes:

*  Operating system (Digital UNIX V3.2C)
*  24 MB parity memory
*  SCSI-2 controller
*  535 MB disk
*  15-inch color monitor
*  ATI Mach64 graphics card
*  Integrated audio and Ethernet
*  NAS 150 license, Open3D license, Communique!, and Multimedia Services
   license (UNIX)
*  Headphone, microphone, mouse, and English user documentation

Workstation options

A full range of PCI/ISA options are available. See the July 1995 Workstation
Systems and Options Catalog Supplement for a complete listing of all
AlphaStation 200 4/100 package systems, available options, and supported
operating systems.

The AlphaStation 200 4/100 package configuration (part number PB410-**) is a
unique system configuration.  For workstation solutions that require custom
configurations, the AlphaStation 200 4/166 and 4/233 systems offer complete
flexibility with SBB (system building block) availability.

