Multimedia Services for AlphaStation Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Enhanced features for Alpha Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX
*  Support for FullVideo Supreme and new FullVideo Supreme JPEG PCI video
   input/output options for Digital UNIX, OpenVMS, and Windows NT
*  Support for the new FullVideo Basic PCI video input option for Windows NT
*  Digital Light & Sound Pack for Windows NT license, media and
   documentation bundled with all Digital Windows NT AlphaStation systems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Multimedia Services products are now available for AlphaStation systems
running the Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1), OpenVMS, or Windows NT
operating systems.

Multimedia Services V1.6 for Digital UNIX, Multimedia Services V1.4 for
OpenVMS, and Digital Light & Sound Pack V1.0 for Windows NT bring audio and
video capabilities to Digital's workstations, and provide a full programming
library for use by developers of new multimedia applications. The products
also provide support for the built-in audio and optional audio/video
hardware on Alpha workstations.

The application programming interface for Multimedia Services for Digital
UNIX and OpenVMS is based on the same Video for Windows multimedia interface
provided in Microsoft Windows NT and Windows 3.1 operating systems. The
three products offer similar, but not identical, capabilities.

Features of these products include:

*  JPEG software compression to create JPEG files without the need of a JPEG
   hardware option (complements JPEG software playback capabilities already
   provided).

*  Intel Indeo R3.1 and R3.2 software decompression and Indeo R3.2
   compression allows users to playback and create one of the most popular
   PC video file formats in the industry. Indeo files created on a PC can
   play on a Digital UNIX AlphaStation system and vice versa.

*  MPEG-1 software decompression in AlphaVCR plays back MPEG-1 audio/video
   files. Users can play files stored in the most popular Internet and
   CD-ROM formats on their AlphaStation systems.

*  AlphaVCR application offers ability to:
   - Play live video and audio
   - Record video in AVI formats including YUV and JPEG
   - Play back audio and video files containing JPEG, Indeo, or YUV data
   - Controls for managing brightness and contrast
   - Play MPEG-1 audio/video files
   - Play AVI files to an output video device like a VCR or TV monitor

*  MEDIACAPTURE from ATI Technologies, Inc., offers features similar to
   AlphaVCR, plus video and editing capabilities.

*  DECsound--an audio record, playback, and edit utility.

