power of the Alpha CPU with no extra hardware. Software video will be used
in areas such as video documentation, presentations, mail, data storage, and
video conferencing. Decompression refers to decompressing and playing back a
video file to the workstation monitor. Compression refers to creating a
compressed video data file from raw video format (YUV 4:2:2).

Highly dependent on the performance of the processor, a 320 x 240 Motion
JPEG file can be displayed at up to 40 frames per second in sample code.
MPEG-1 and Indeo playback is faster. In addition, Digital's patented
AccuVideo rendering techniques significantly enhance the perceptual image
quality of the video. MPEG-1, JPEG, and Indeo files displayed with AlphaVCR
in Multimedia Services look better on a AlphaStation system than other
workstations or personal computers.

