Video Conferencing and Collaborative Computing Software

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Collaborative software application supports multiple users in realtime
   interactive sessions
*  Provides highest quality video conferencing available on AlphaStation
   systems
*  Interoperable between Windows, Windows NT, and Digital UNIX systems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital will now resell Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) and Windows NT
versions of InSoft, Inc.'s Communique!--a LAN/WAN based multiplatform
software application for video conferencing and software collaboration--as
Communique! Step Up. In addition, Digital will bundle a collaboration only
version of Communique!, called Communique! Starter, on AlphaStation systems
running Digital UNIX or Windows NT. Communique! Starter allows multiple
users to access a whiteboard and interactively annotate and save graphic
images in realtime.

Communique! Starter

Communique! Starter is a collaborative software application aimed at target
markets including CASE, ECAD/MCAD, scientific visualization, healthcare,
geographic information systems, process control, entertainment, broadcast,
and finance. Communique! Starter includes separate modules for:

*  Shared Whiteboard--provides screen captures and conversion of graphic
   images, including: Sun Raster, Encapsulated PS, GIF, TIFF, JPEG, Windows
   BMP, PCX, and TARGA. Session attendees can pan and zoom, copy and paste,
   annotate, and save any of the above supported graphic formats while
   involved in the session.

*  Chat Tool--a text based multiuser realtime communication software
   component that can be used in conjunction with Shared Whiteboard or used
   as a standalone application.

*  Conference Manager--establishes and controls the conference using IP
   addresses. It provides interactive scanning of the network for users,
   handles lost connections or network changes, and allows up to 24 people
   in a conference at one time. Each user can customize the conference
   manager to use only those plug-ins (Chat Tool and Shared Whiteboard) that
   they need.

*  Business Card Editor--allows the user to create a personal business card
   with photo icon (video capture not provided on systems not equipped with
   appropriate hardware). All modules layer on the InSoft OpenDVE (digital
   video everywhere) API. OpenDVE is available from InSoft as a developer's
   toolkit. Using OpenDVE, users can customize the conferencing environment
   by developing in-house applications that take advantage of Communique!.

As a LAN solution, Communique! Starter supports TCP/IP, Ethernet, and/or
FDDI. The WAN strategy allows for digital video between ATM, Frame Relay,
ISDN, and SMDS. The application interface is consistent from vendor to
vendor allowing users to avoid learning curve delays when they decide to
implement new high performance systems like Alpha.

Communique! Step Up--Value Upgrade Kit

Communique! Step Up--Value is Digital's Windows NT video conferencing
upgrade kit that provides a low cost video conferencing option for
AlphaStation systems. This product includes all of the necessary components
for implementing a desktop video conferencing system. The Value kit includes
Digital's low cost FullVideo Basic PCI bus video capture board, a single
slot PCI option that supports graphics independent video capture at up to
320x240 pixels. The kit also includes the Toshiba desktop camera. This
camera includes a tilt and swivel base, auto white balance and composite
output, AC adapter, and necessary video cable. Communique! Step Up software
adds audio and video conferencing to the collaborative software of
Communique! Starter.

Communique! Step Up--Premium Upgrade Kit

Communique! Step Up--Premium is Digital's UNIX video conferencing upgrade
kit that provides the highest quality video conferencing available on
AlphaStation systems. This product has all of the necessary components for
implementing a desktop video conferencing system, including Digital's high
performance FullVideo Supreme JPEG PCI bus video capture board, a single
slot PCI option that supports JPEG compression and decompression of digital
video, video input, and video output at up to 640x480 pixels. The kit also
includes the Toshiba desktop camera. This camera includes a tilt and swivel
base, auto white, balance and composite output, AC adapter, and necessary
video cable. Desktop speakers from Koss provide front panel microphone and
headphone access and include volume control. The Koss speakers will also be
offered as a standalone product in the near future. Communique! Step Up
includes audio and video conferencing, as well as collaborative software
like a graphical whiteboard and text chat tool.

Team Machine configuration

The Team Machine configuration integrates the Communique! Step Up--Premium
kit components with the AlphaStation 200 4/100 workstation, providing
competitively priced configuration with out-of-the-box video conferencing
capabilities. (Refer to the "UNIX Package Option for AlphaStation 200 4/100
Workstation" article in this issue for additional platform information.)

