Midrange 3D Graphics Accelerators for AlphaStation Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Offers fastest PLBsurf performance under $15K
*  Two midrange 3D graphics accelerators to suit users' specific needs
*  Optimized solids modeling graphics for MCAD, MCAE, GIS, and molecular
   modeling

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The ZLXp-L family of graphics accelerators--the ZLXp-L1 and ZLXp-L2--are new
midrange, 3D, solids modeling graphics options for AlphaStation systems.

Both the ZLXp-L1 and ZLXp-L2 offer 24 bits per pixel double buffered (can
display 16.7 million colors simultaneously), 4 overlay planes, 8 stencil
planes, and a full 24-bit Z buffer that offers excellent solid model
rendering, which is so important in many 3D applications.

The ZLXp-L1 has 16 MB of RAM and one rendering engine, and requires one PCI
slot. The ZLXp-L2 has 32 MB of RAM, two rendering engines, and plugs into
one PCI slot but requires two slots because the daughter card extends over
into a second slot. The ZLXp-L2 offers up to 50 percent higher performance
than the ZLXp-L1 due to the increased RAM and the additional rendering
engine.

In addition to supporting standard 3D primitives such as gouraud shaded
triangles, the ZLXp-L family provides support for more advanced graphics
objects and techniques such as anti-aliased vectors, accumulation buffering,
transparency, and stereoscopic viewing. The advanced graphics techniques of
accumulation buffering and transparency are done in software with the
ZLXp-L1, but are truly optimized with the ZLXp-L2 as they are done in
hardware.

BENEFITS

The ZLXp-L graphics accelerators offer superb price/performance in the
midrange 3D graphics space. The combination of excellent price/performance
of the ZLXp-L graphics accelerators and the industry leading CPU performance
of AlphaStation systems offers users increased productivity and improved
time to market by allowing them to display, manipulate, and edit 3D design
objects with excellent graphics and system response time and powerful
features.

The true color capability and full 24-bit Z buffer available with both ZLX-L
graphics accelerators provides support for many 3D applications, including
midrange mechanical CAD and CAE, molecular modeling, GIS, and scientific
visualization.

