Concurrent Use Licenses for OpenVMS and Digital UNIX

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Concurrent Use Licenses are now available for the Digital UNIX (all
   versions) and OpenVMS (V6.2) operating systems
*  Concurrent Use Licenses can be used with any hardware platform running
   the same operating system

DESCRIPTION

With the introduction of Concurrent Use Licenses for OpenVMS and Digital
UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) software, license choices for Digital's
operating systems become as simple as that for layered products. A
Concurrent Use License permits interactive use for a specified number of
users. The Traditional Unlimited License permits unlimited interactive use
for a specified system. Note that the Operating System Base License is a
prerequisite to both license types.

Support for previous versions

Concurrent Use Licenses for Digital UNIX work with the current and prior
versions of the software. Concurrent Use Licenses for OpenVMS software work
on OpenVMS Alpha V1.5 and V6.1, but these versions do not support mixed VAX
and Alpha clusters.

Concurrent Use Licenses for OpenVMS software do not work on OpenVMS VAX
prior to V6.2, unless the group table patch is installed (see "Extending
user benefits" section below).

The following licenses will remain available for those who wish to add users
to prior versions of OpenVMS VAX software:

*  QL-XUL**-B* -- Individual Interactive User License for OpenVMS VAX V5.5
   or later
*  QL-09S**-B* -- Distributed Interactive User License for OpenVMS VAX V6.0
   or later

Impact to existing Interactive User Licenses

All Interactive User Licenses will continue to work on new versions of the
operating system. In addition, the Distributed Interactive User Licenses
will work across hardware platforms and support mixed VAX and Alpha clusters
with OpenVMS V6.2.

Extending user benefits

Digital is making an OpenVMS group table patch available to enable
Concurrent Use Licenses to work on mixed VAX and Alpha clusters (as well as
individual systems and single architecture clusters) running:

*  OpenVMS Alpha V6.1
*  OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2, V6.0, and V6.1

When installed on the software versions above, the patch will also permit
the Distributed Interactive User Licenses (QL-MT3**-B* and QL-09S**-B*) to
support mixed VAX and Alpha clusters. The right to use these licenses in
this manner is a courtesy extended by Digital. The OpenVMS group table patch
may be duplicated and used with each valid Concurrent Use or Distributed
Interactive User License for OpenVMS software. Users may install and use the
patch under their existing license agreements.

This patch can be obtained in the following manners:

*  On the Internet; users may identify the location of software patches by
   referencing the MCS Home Page: http://www.digital.com/info/mcs.
*  Ordered as a separate kit; order number is QA-MT3AC-H8.
*  On the August 1995 OpenVMS Alpha Consolidated Distribution CD-ROM and the
   September 1995 OpenVMS VAX Consolidated Distribution CD-ROM.
*  On TIMA services database.

BENEFITS

*  License type choice is now the same as for layered products.
*  Supports mixed VAX and Alpha clusters with OpenVMS V6.2.
*  Users can trade-up to Concurrent Use Licenses from either an Unlimited
   Interactive User License (QL-XUL**-6*, QL-MT2**-6*,  QL-MT7**-6*) or from
   an Unlimited Traditional License (QL-XUL**-AA, QL-MT2**-AA, QL-MT7**-AA).
*  Concurrent Use Licenses provide more capability for the same price as
   Interactive User Licenses.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

