POLYCENTER Capacity Planner V3.0a

HIGHLIGHTS

*  Supports the Digital UNIX operating system and provides capacity planning
   for a multi-platform networked client/server environment
*  Maintains systems and network performance to ensure availability and
   enable resource planning
*  Allows choice of a product or service to fulfill capacity planning needs
*  Uses a graphical modeling interface that supports dynamic "what-if"
   analysis

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The POLYCENTER Capacity Planner tool allows the system manager to define the
system's total workload in terms of manageable units, and then report
against that information. Workloads and groups of workloads are used in
model generation and can be reported against in the Capacity Planner reports
or graphics. Workloads can be defined according to users, images, UICs (User
Identification Controls), process name, account name, and process mode in
the context of the particular operating system.

BENEFITS

*  State-of-the-art modeling -- Includes a graphical modeling interface from
   which "what-if" analysis can be performed dynamically.
*  Supports various network protocols -- OSI/DECnet, TCP/IP, UDP/IP,
   IPX/SPX, and LAT protocols.
*  Supports diverse operating systems -- OpenVMS VAX, OpenVMS Alpha, and
   Digital UNIX (formerly called DEC OSF/1) operating systems.
*  Ease of use -- The Motif interface provides system modeling; a "what-if"
   scenario can be performed with one mouse click.
*  Reporting -- Summary or detailed reports can be generated on various
   performance statistics, including resource utilization, response time,
   throughput, queue link, and service time. Performance information is
   available for each CPU, HSC storage device, disk, channel, adapter, CI or
   Ethernet bus, or Token Ring for current and projected workloads or
   configurations. Performance data for extended LAN components, including
   bridges, routers, and brouters is also available.
*  Data collection -- Utilizes data collected by the POLYCENTER Performance
   Solution Data Collectors for OpenVMS VAX and Alpha systems; the
   POLYCENTER Performance Monitor Data Collector for Digital UNIX systems;
   and the new built-in data collector on PATHWORKS V5.0c.
*  Change management -- POLYCENTER Capacity Planner allows users to make
   educated strategic decisions in their IT environments. Whether users are
   moving to a client/server computing environment, downsizing, upsizing, or
   rightsizing, the Capacity Planner can act as a change management vehicle
   for their IT systems as they plan system resource requirements for
   today's and tomorrow's needs.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

POLYCENTER Capacity Planner V3.0a is available now.

